{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Sixth turn: answering the registered applicability gap with a much smaller, legible contrast harness (draft/assurance_gap.rs) that holds every input equal except the Entry type's Snapshot::use_snapshots(). It exercises one responder node through the same legal leader prefix (Prepare, AcceptSync of six entries with decided_idx 6, forwarded Compaction::Trim(6)) and then the same legal Prepare from a node whose decided index is 3 with an older accepted round, which is the message whose handling builds the log update. Run locally first: the non-snapshot case aborts with 'attempt to subtract with overflow' while the snapshot-enabled case completes, so the experiment is submitted to bound the asserted defect with measured evidence rather than leaving the gap open.\\\",\n  \\\"experiment\\\": {\n    \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-question-0\\\",\n    \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"assurance_gap.rs\\\",\n    \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n      \\\"follower_prepare\\\",\n      \\\"logsync\\\",\n      \\\"memstorage_suffix\\\",\n      \\\"storage_get_suffix_contract\\\",\n      \\\"sync_log\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"scope\\\": {\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Two single-node scenarios in one test: a responder replica is driven through a legal leader prefix (Prepare, AcceptSync with six entries and decided_idx 6, forwarded Compaction::Trim(6)) and then receives a legal Prepare with decided_idx 3 and an older accepted round. Everything is held equal except the Entry type: one scenario has Snapshot::use_snapshots() == false, the other true. The outcome of handling that Prepare is reported per case.\\\",\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n        \\\"The messages delivered are the shapes a real leader produces (Prepare, AcceptSync/log_sync, forwarded Compaction::Trim, and a later Prepare from a node whose decided index lags); the responder is a real OmniPaxos instance whose state is produced by those messages rather than set directly.\\\",\n        \\\"The three-node configuration is used only for construction; the responder is node 2 and the sender is node 1. No tick, no election and no message routing are involved, so nothing depends on scheduling.\\\",\n        \\\"AcceptSync carries sync_idx 0 with a six-entry suffix and decided_idx 6, i.e. the update a leader sends to a peer that has no entries yet; the forwarded Trim(6) is legal because the responder's decided index is already 6.\\\",\n        \\\"The state this harness reaches (accepted_idx 6, decided_idx 6, compacted_idx 6, accepted round newer than the preparing node's) is the same state the earlier multi-node experiment reached through real message exchange.\\\",\n        \\\"Dev profile with overflow checks enabled, matching the controller's cargo test invocation.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"excluded\\\": [\n        \\\"Release-profile behaviour, the persistent storage backend, and cluster-level consequences after the abort are not measured here.\\\",\n        \\\"Only the snapshot/non-snapshot distinction is varied; cluster size, batch size, trim index and quorum are held equal.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"parameters\\\": {\n        \\\"responder_pid\\\": 2,\n        \\\"sender_pid\\\": 1,\n        \\\"entries_synced\\\": 6,\n        \\\"trim_idx\\\": 6,\n        \\\"stale_decided_idx\\\": 3,\n        \\\"cases\\\": [\\\"nosnapshot_entry\\\", \\\"snapshot_entry\\\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"scenario(case, snapshots) builds one OmniPaxos instance (pid 2, nodes 1,2,3, MemoryStorage behind a shared handle) and then calls, in order: handle_incoming(Prepare{n: (1,1,pid 1), decided_idx: 0, n_accepted: 0, accepted_idx: 0}) so the responder promises at ballot (1,1,pid 1) and enters (Follower, Prepare); handle_incoming(AcceptSync{n: (1,1,pid 1), seq_num: (session 0, counter 1), decided_idx: 6, log_sync: {decided_snapshot: None, suffix: six entries 0..5, sync_idx: 0, stopsign: None}}) so it accepts six entries and records decided_idx 6; handle_incoming(Compaction::Trim(6)) so its decided prefix is compacted. The harness then emits state_reached (accepted_idx, decided_idx, compacted_idx) and finally calls handle_incoming(Prepare{n: (1,2,pid 1), decided_idx: 3, n_accepted: 0, accepted_idx: 6}) inside catch_unwind, emitting log_sync_outcome with outcome, panic message and the three indices. The test runs this twice: case nosnapshot_entry (Entry::Snapshot::use_snapshots() == false) and case snapshot_entry (use_snapshots() == true, a max-value snapshot type).\\\",\n    \\\"semantic_changes\\\": [\n      \\\"No production logic is replaced or patched; the harness only uses the crate's public API and message types.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"responsibility\\\": \\\"The contrast isolates which captured component decides the outcome: the core's log-update construction selects its branch from T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() and the deciding node's decided index, and the captured in-memory storage implementation aborts on an index below its trimmed prefix.\\\",\n    \\\"previous_id\\\": \\\"8cb68564d0514352a61204d7c6be6f3c-experiment\\\",\n    \\\"revision_reason\\\": \\\"New harness file and a second case: the earlier experiment used a full three-node cluster with a crash-recovered node and non-snapshot entries; this one keeps the same request but adds a snapshot-capable Entry type and supplies the leader prefix directly so the applicability boundary can be measured with the rest held equal.\\\",\n    \\\"prerequisites\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"alias\\\": \\\"admitted_nosnap\\\",\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"state_reached\\\",\n        \\\"conditions\\\": [\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"case\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"nosnapshot_entry\\\" },\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"accepted_idx\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 6 },\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"decided_idx\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 6 },\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"compacted_idx\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 6 }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"alias\\\": \\\"admitted_snap\\\",\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"state_reached\\\",\n        \\\"conditions\\\": [\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"case\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"snapshot_entry\\\" },\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"accepted_idx\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 6 },\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"decided_idx\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 6 },\n          { \\\"field\\\": \\\"compacted_idx\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 6 }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \\\"comparisons\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"log_sync_outcome\\\",\n        \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"case\\\", \\\"use_snapshots\\\"],\n        \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"admitted_nosnap\\\",\n        \\\"assertion\\\": { \\\"field\\\": \\\"outcome\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"completed\\\" },\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Without snapshots, handling the stale node's Prepare completes instead of aborting.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"log_sync_outcome\\\",\n        \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"case\\\", \\\"use_snapshots\\\"],\n        \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"admitted_snap\\\",\n        \\\"assertion\\\": { \\\"field\\\": \\\"outcome\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"completed\\\" },\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"With snapshots enabled, the same request completes, bounding the failure to the non-snapshot configuration.\\\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-knowledge-0\\\",\n        \\\"revision\\\": 1,\n        \\\"assertion\\\": \\\"the snapshot branch is taken only when use_snapshots() is true and decided_idx > common_prefix_idx; otherwise get_suffix(common_prefix_idx) is used with no comparison against the responder's compacted index\\\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
